      "paragraph_id": 1,
      "original": "Last week I gone to the city with my cousin’s, we was planning to watch a movie but the cinema tickets was already sold out so we decide to just walking around the mall instead. The mall was very crowded, people keeps bumping into us and the music was to loud that we can barely hear each other. We stoped at a clothing store where my cousin tryed on some shirt’s, but none of them fits him good. After that, we seen a small café and sit down for coffee and dessert. I order a latte but the waiter bring me a capuccino, I didn’t want to complane so I drink it anyways. While we was eating, a group of teenagers sat on the table next too us and they was making alot of noise, which made it hard to relax. When we finally finish, we was suppose to take the bus home but we miss it because we was talking too much. So we end up walking half the way until we find a taxi, by then we was already tired and our feets was hurting badly. Even though everything didn’t goes as we plan, the day turn out to be fun and memorable, we was laughing about it the whole way home.",
      "proofread": "Last week I went to the city with my cousin; we were planning to watch a movie, but the cinema tickets were already sold out, so we decided to just walk around the mall instead. The mall was very crowded; people kept bumping into us, and the music was too loud that we could barely hear each other. We stopped at a clothing store where my cousin tried on some shirts, but none of them fit him well. After that, we saw a small café and sat down for coffee and dessert. I ordered a latte, but the waiter brought me a cappuccino. I didn’t want to complain, so I drank it anyway. While we were eating, a group of teenagers sat at the table next to us, and they were making a lot of noise, which made it hard to relax. When we finally finished, we were supposed to take the bus home, but we missed it because we were talking too much. So we ended up walking half the way until we found a taxi; by then, we were already tired, and our feet were hurting badly. Even though everything didn’t go as we planned, the day turned out to be fun and memorable; we were laughing about it the whole way home.",
